कास 2. कास, अस्, अम्, m. n. (for काश), a
species of reed or long grass, Saccharum Spontaneum;
another plant, Hyperanthera Moringa.

कशिपु कशिपु, उस्, उ, m. n. a mat; a pillow;
(उस्), m. food; clothing; (ऊ), du. food and clothing;
(sometimes spelt कसिपु; cf. हिरण्य-कशिपु.)
—कशिपूपबर्हण (˚पु-उप्˚), अम्, n., Ved. a
cover of a pillow, cloth.

कसनोत्पाटन कसनोत्पाटन, अस्, m. the
plant Gendarussa Vulgaris; (perhaps a wrong reading
for कासनोत्प्˚.)

काश्यपेय, अस्, m. (a patronymic fr. कश्यप),
an epithet of the twelve Ādityas; also of the sun;
and of Garuḍa, the bird of Viṣṇu.

कासुन्दीवटिका, f. a remedy against cough, an
acid preparation, a mixture of tamarinds and mustard;
(perhaps a wrong reading for कासन्दी˚.)
